WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:11.539
"According to Alpha, UserPFM5 lives this way," Ally said as she and Mateo walked across town.

2
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.135
"I don't know what I would have done without you and Alpha," Mateo said.

3
00:00:16.136 --> 00:00:21.090
"I'm glad we could help. I know how much you want that comic," Ally said.

4
00:00:21.091 --> 00:00:29.581
"And as Alpha said, powers or not, I'm still an Astralian, and it's my prime directive to be helpful.

5
00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:32.497
Plus, I enjoy being helpful.

6
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.708
My parents would be surprised to hear that."

7
00:00:35.709 --> 00:00:39.195
"I hope I get to meet them one day," Mateo said.

8
00:00:39.196 --> 00:00:42.273
"Then I can tell them how helpful you've been to me."

9
00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:44.498
"That would be nice."

10
00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:47.304
Mateo suddenly froze.

11
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:53.382
"Now that I'm going to be face-to-face with UserPFM5, I'm super nervous.

12
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:57.727
What if this person gets mad at me for tracking the address?"

13
00:00:57.728 --> 00:01:06.299
"Just explain how you've always wanted this comic, and I bet UserPFM5 will sell it to you," Ally said.

14
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:13.542
"Ask nicely, and if UserPFM5 says no, say thank you, and we'll leave."

15
00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:17.073
Ally looked down at the address on her phone.

16
00:01:17.074 --> 00:01:23.988
"We have to turn here, onto Cactus Road."

17
00:01:23.989 --> 00:01:27.934
"That's funny," Mateo said.

18
00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:30.754
"This is Bethany's street.

19
00:01:30.755 --> 00:01:33.215
I wonder if she knows the buyer of the comic book.

20
00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:34.970
I should ask her about it."

21
00:01:34.971 --> 00:01:37.559
"Good idea," Ally said.

22
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:44.483
While Mateo took out his phone, Ally walked off, looking for the right house.

23
00:01:44.484 --> 00:01:49.961
"Wait, Ally!" Mateo was still trying to text Bethany.

24
00:01:49.962 --> 00:01:53.406
"I don't even know if she's back from vacation yet."

25
00:01:53.407 --> 00:01:57.270
"So ask her," Ally said as she rang the doorbell.

26
00:01:57.271 --> 00:02:01.427
"I will. But . . ." Mateo looked confused.

27
00:02:01.428 --> 00:02:03.794
"Why did you stop here?"

28
00:02:03.795 --> 00:02:08.458
"Because this is 1232 Cactus Road, silly," Ally said.

29
00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:10.814
"Alpha said that this is where UserPF—"

30
00:02:10.815 --> 00:02:14.359
The door flew open, and there was Bethany.

31
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.479
"Hi!" Bethany said. "I was going to text you, Mateo.

32
00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.963
We got back from our trip a little while ago. Come on in."

33
00:02:23.964 --> 00:02:29.025
"No thank you," Mateo said coldly.

34
00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:31.395
Bethany looked confused.

35
00:02:31.396 --> 00:02:36.371
"Are you mad at me? I told you I couldn't text while I was away.

36
00:02:36.372 --> 00:02:41.334
My dad never lets us use our devices while we are on vacation."

37
00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:46.790
"Yes, I'm mad, but not about that!" Mateo crossed his arms.

38
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.881
"You're UserPFM5!"

39
00:02:49.882 --> 00:02:54.123
Bethany blushed. "How did you know?"

40
00:02:54.124 --> 00:02:59.150
"Alpha . . . I mean, my new computer figured it out," Ally said. "What?"

41
00:02:59.151 --> 00:03:04.961
Bethany blinked in surprise. "How is that possible?" "Um,

42
00:03:04.962 --> 00:03:09.693
I bought the best computer at the store," Ally said quickly. Bethany

43
00:03:09.694 --> 00:03:14.440
still looked confused, but Mateo was scowling at her. "How

44
00:03:14.441 --> 00:03:18.302
could you do this to me, Bethany?" he snapped. "I

45
00:03:18.303 --> 00:03:21.569
just wanted to surprise you," Bethany said. Mateo

46
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.838
scowled. "Surprise me?" "I

47
00:03:25.839 --> 00:03:34.950
knew how much you wanted the first Cosmic Quest comic, but I didn't want you to spend all your prize money on it," Bethany said. "So

48
00:03:34.951 --> 00:03:39.896
I bought it for you using my prize money. I

49
00:03:39.897 --> 00:03:45.338
put in a high bid that I knew would win the auction." She smiled. "UserPFM5

50
00:03:45.339 --> 00:03:51.362
stands for Present for Mateo." "Wow!

51
00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:58.702
That's so nice, Bethany!" Ally beamed. "Isn't it, Mateo?" But

52
00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:03.634
Mateo just stood there. Ally

53
00:04:03.635 --> 00:04:07.496
nudged him with her elbow. "Isn't it?" "Yes!"

54
00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:14.892
he finally said. "This is the nicest thing that anyone's ever done for me." "I'm

55
00:04:14.893 --> 00:04:18.871
sorry I made you worry, Mateo," Bethany said. "The

56
00:04:18.872 --> 00:04:21.690
comic arrived a few minutes ago. I

57
00:04:21.691 --> 00:04:26.878
was going to wrap it, but since you're here, do you want to see it?" Mateo

58
00:04:26.879 --> 00:04:33.965
grinned. "You bet I do!" Bethany

59
00:04:33.966 --> 00:04:37.743
grabbed Mateo's hand and pulled him inside. "Come

60
00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:43.348
on, Ally! You can look at it too. It's awesome!" "That's

61
00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.515
okay," Ally said. "I've

62
00:04:45.516 --> 00:04:51.559
got lots of stuff to do at home. See you later, Mateo." Ally

63
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.437
turned to leave. "Well,

64
00:04:54.438 --> 00:04:58.665
Alpha fixed one problem," she thought. "Here's

65
00:04:58.666 --> 00:05:07.117
hoping she can solve my passport problem next!" ***

66
00:05:07.118 --> 00:05:10.849
As soon as Ally got home, she pressed Alpha's power button.

67
00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:15.286
"Okay, Alpha, wake up. Let's get to work."

68
00:05:15.287 --> 00:05:18.611
But Alpha didn't respond.

69
00:05:18.612 --> 00:05:21.642
"I said, wake up, Alpha!"

70
00:05:21.643 --> 00:05:27.443
When there was still no response, Ally pushed the button again, and then again.

71
00:05:27.444 --> 00:05:35.527
"Oh no. She's broken again. This is worse than worse!" Ally wailed.

72
00:05:35.528 --> 00:05:41.824
"Now I'm going to have to call Lainie and tell her I can't make the trip to view the eclipse!"

73
00:05:41.825 --> 00:05:49.565
"Eight more years on Earth . . . that's like ten years on Astralia!"

74
00:05:49.566 --> 00:05:53.566
Ally sank down onto her bed, trying to console herself.

75
00:05:53.567 --> 00:06:01.543
"Maybe the years will go by quickly. At least I have a job here and friends and . . ."

76
00:06:01.544 --> 00:06:10.629
Brushing away a few tears, she picked up her phone and dialed Lainie's assistant.

